        "thinking": "I'm working through the root दृङ् with वि prefix, considering how the desiderative सन् attaches and whether इट् augment is optional here per the rules governing ṛ-ending roots.\n\nChecking 7.2.12, दृ counts as ugantas, so iṭ would normally be blocked, but then I recall 7.2.75 \"किरश्च पञ्चभ्यः\" specifically lists दृङ् among five roots that take iṭ in the desiderative despite that general prohibition — so the form should indeed include the augment.\n\nDefaulting to parasmaipada since the fruit goes to another, not the agent, I get विदिदरिषयेः for the second person singular vidhiliṅ. That's my answer: विदिदरिषयेः.\n\n",
